Tested-by: Luis Chamberlain <mcgrof@kernel.org>
Cc: Zi Yan <ziy@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by incorrectly setting search marks on all entries in a newly created node when splitting an entry that had search marks set. This behavior was appropriate for splits to order 0 but led to incorrect mark propagation when splitting to a larger order, as sibling entries should not inherit these marks.

Here is the patch:

+static inline void node_mark_slots(struct xa_node *node, unsigned int sibs,
